From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:56:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 48/57] panvk: Fold replicating geometry shaders by replaying
 the draw (06n-arch)

Unreal Engine 4 under D3D12 (Deep Rock Galactic, vkd3d-proton) also has
a GS that emits each input triangle 6 times, one copy per cube face,
with gl_Layer and one more output set to the copy index. 0019 refuses
it, the pipeline fails and UE4's D3D12 RHI treats that as fatal ("out
of memory").

Generalize the pass-through matcher: the GS may emit the input
primitive up to 8 times, ended between copies, and each output may be
a constant that only depends on the copy instead of a copy of the
vertex's input. The folded VS computes those constants from a copy
index (load_invocation_id, lowered to a new vs.gs_copy sysval), the VS
shader records the copy count (serialized with it), and panvk_cmd_draw
replays each draw that many times with the copy index set. That is what
the GS did: every copy of every primitive, each on its own layer, for
the same amount of vertex shading. Indirect draws are replayed the same
way.
